+
+    Writes are crash-safe: the new state is first written and synced to a
+    journal file next to the database (``<path>.journal``), then written over
+    the database file in place, and finally the journal is removed. If the
+    process dies while writing the database file, the next read restores it
+    from the journal; if it dies while writing the journal, the database file
+    is still intact and the incomplete journal is discarded.
+
+    The database file is never replaced by renaming another file over it, so
+    its inode stays the same.
